    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "A paused owner reproduces the stale-write hazard in a local lab.",
      "narration": "In a disposable two worker lab, pause the old owner beyond its lease. Let a successor acquire ownership and write, then resume the old process.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Reproduce stale work",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sh",
          "text": "kill -STOP \"$old_leader_pid\"\n# Wait for lease expiry and new owner.\n# Verify successor has written token 42.\nkill -CONT \"$old_leader_pid\"",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "A pause simulates stale ownership",
            "Record token and result for every write"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10500,
      "caption": "The token check must be atomic with the protected mutation.",
      "narration": "Give each acquisition a monotonically increasing token from the coordination system. Storage checks it atomically with each mutation; checking only in the client leaves a race.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Fence at storage",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "text": "-- Example resource already has token 42\nUPDATE resource\nSET value = 'old', fence = 41\nWHERE id = 1 AND fence <= 41\nRETURNING id;\n-- Expected: zero rows",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Persist the highest accepted token",
            "Do not generate tokens from wall clocks"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "caption": "The old request must fail after the newer token is accepted.",
      "narration": "Assert that the stale write changes nothing after token forty two has been accepted. Every mutation path must enforce fencing, including external side effects and background jobs.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
